PKG(1)                      User Commands                    PKG(1)

NAME
    pkg - install, remove, list and build packages

SYNOPSIS
    pkg [--prefix dir] [--root dir] install file...
    pkg [--prefix dir] [--root dir] check file...
    pkg [--prefix dir] remove [--force] name...
    pkg [--prefix dir] list
    pkg [--prefix dir] info name|file
    pkg [--prefix dir] verify [name...]
    pkg [--root dir] build dir [file]

DESCRIPTION
    pkg installs applications from package files into /home/.local and
    keeps a record of every installed file. A package is a gzip
    compressed ustar archive named name-version.mpk whose first member
    is the manifest and whose files lie under files/, relative to the
    prefix. Every check of an installation runs before anything is
    written: the dependencies, the conflicts, the shared libraries with
    their ABI numbers and symbols, and the ownership of every path.

COMMANDS
    install   install or upgrade the packages in the named files
    check     run the checks of install without writing anything
    remove    remove installed packages; --force removes a package that
              other packages depend on
    list      print the installed packages, one name, version and
              summary per line
    info      print the manifest and the files of an installed package
              or of a package file
    verify    compare the recorded size and checksum of every installed
              file with the file on disk
    build     write a package from a directory holding manifest and
              files/; the needs lines are derived from the ELF files

OPTIONS
    --prefix dir   install under dir instead of /home/.local
    --root dir     read lib/abi and the system libraries below dir

BUNDLED APPLICATIONS
    Optional applications are available as archives in /usr/share/packages.
    Install selected archives, or all of them, with the examples below.
    They are not installed automatically. The package prefix persists on
    the data volume across root image rebuilds.

FILES
    /home/.local/lib/pkg/name/manifest   the manifest as installed
    /home/.local/lib/pkg/name/files      path, size and CRC-32 of each file
    /home/.local/lib/pkg/name/dirs       the directories the package created
    /home/.local/share/launcher          launcher entries of the packages
    /home/.local/share/mime.types        MIME types of the packages
    /home/.local/share/mime.apps         MIME handlers of the packages
    /lib/abi                             ABI numbers of the system libraries

EXAMPLES
    pkg install /usr/share/packages/calc-*.mpk
    pkg install /usr/share/packages/*.mpk
    pkg build pong
    pkg install pong-1.2.0.mpk
    pkg list
    pkg remove pong

SEE ALSO
    tar(1), gzip(1), ld(1)
